<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=lateen-sail">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Transport and navigation</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lateen sail</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">2nd century CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century">2nd century</a> · Also known as Lateen, Latin rig</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A lateen is a triangular sail set on a long yard mounted at an angle on the mast and running fore and aft; it originated in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> as early as the 2nd century CE, in Roman times. It became common there by the 5th century and by the 6th had largely replaced the square sail, a change suggested to have been made on cost grounds, as the two rigs performed much alike. Arab seafarers adopted it after the Muslim conquests, and it later rigged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caravel">caravels</a> and the mizzens of full-rigged ships.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lateen-sail.jpg" alt="Lateen sail" width="320" height="168" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Meister der Predigten des Heiligen Gregor von Nazianz · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Meister_der_Predigten_des_Heiligen_Gregor_von_Nazianz_001.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>2nd century CE</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>The Mediterranean</dd></div><div><dt>Credited to</dt><dd><a href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a></dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>An older view gave it an eastern origin, in Arab seafaring.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/sail">Sail<span>6th millennium BCE</span></a></div><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Led to</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/caravel">Caravel<span>c. 1255</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=lateen-sail">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
